// @expect-error An external block is always private to its file, so it takes no modifier such as 'public'. Remove 'public', and call its functions from Ens functions that other files can use.
// External functions are never shared through a visibility modifier; the block stays private
// to its file and its behavior is shared by wrapping the calls in Ens functions.
public external from libc {
    abs(int x) -> int;
}

main() -> int {
    return abs(-1);
}
